  "response": "Aluminium cans are widely used in food storage due to their lightweight, durability, and ability to preserve food. They are commonly used for storing liquids, powdered goods, and snacks. The sealed nature of the cans helps prevent contamination and maintains freshness. Aluminium is also recyclable, making it an environmentally friendly choice. However, they are not suitable for storing acidic or highly reactive foods, as they can leach aluminium into the food. The use of aluminium cans has been widely accepted in the food industry due to their efficiency and cost-effectiveness."
